// ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  01 — Hello World & Statement Terminators                    ║
// ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
//
// Every statement in GOM ends with a confidence terminator:
//   !    normal confidence
//   !!   high confidence
//   !!!  absolute confidence
//   ?    debug terminator (prints debug info to stderr)
//
// All confidence levels execute — they express intent, not behavior.

// The simplest GOM program:
print "Hello, Gulf of Mexico!"!

// Higher confidence terminators work identically:
print "I am fairly sure about this."!!
print "I am ABSOLUTELY sure about this."!!!

// Multiple prints on separate lines:
print "Welcome to GOM"!
print "An experimental language"!
print "with unique features."!

// Numbers work too:
print 42!

// Floating point:
print 3.14159!
